course: dictionary
lesson: 1408
title: Cardiologist: the heart doctor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cardiologist is a doctor who is an expert in the heart and blood vessels. Blood vessels are the tubes that carry blood around your body. When the heart has a problem, a cardiologist is the doctor who helps. «Some children are born with heart conditions, and heart doctors called cardiologists decide which sports are safe.» The words heart doctors are the clue: a cardiologist is a heart doctor.
explain: Look inside the long word. Cardio- means heart, and -ologist means an expert who studies something. Put them together and you get an expert in the heart. This trick works for other long words too, so always ask: what is this word made of?
explain: Cardiologists check the heart with tools. A stethoscope lets them listen to the heartbeat. An ECG is a heart tracing, a picture of the heart's signals on paper. An ultrasound scan helps them see inside the body. If you read about a cardiologist, you know the problem is with the heart.
fact: A cardiologist is a doctor who is an expert in the heart and blood vessels.
fact: Cardio- means heart, so a cardiologist is a heart doctor.
fact: Cardiologists check the heart with tools like a stethoscope, an ECG (heart tracing) and an ultrasound scan.
fact: A cardiologist is a hospital specialist, so you may hear about one in a careers talk.
exercise: What is a cardiologist? | A coach who runs races | *A doctor who is an expert in the heart and blood vessels | A teacher who draws pictures of hearts | A nurse who works in a shop
exercise: In «heart doctors called cardiologists», which words are the clue to what a cardiologist is? | safe | decide | *heart doctors | sports
exercise: Which tool do cardiologists use to listen to the heart? | A paintbrush | *A stethoscope | A ruler | A football
test: A cardiologist mostly treats problems with which part of the body? | The teeth | The knee | The eyes | *The heart
test: The word cardiologist starts with cardio. What does cardio mean? | Lung | Brain | *Heart | Bone
exam: Why would a child with a heart condition see a cardiologist before playing sport? | To learn to read faster | *To find out which sports are safe for them | To buy new football boots | To get a stethoscope as a birthday present
